Findings:
=========

Audit RULES OUT 3 hypotheses and pin-points the wedge to ANS distributions
inside hf_global (NOT in coefficient orders or LZ77).

1. dequant matrix bytes: 1 byte ours vs cjxl across ALL cells (just an
   all_default=1 flag — bit-identical).

2. block context map count (W44-39): at parity (already known).

3. num_hf_presets: ours=1, cjxl varies (1 at d>=3 patches cells, 2 at d=1,2).

4. used_orders bitmask:
     ours = 0x55 (pop=4, buckets {DCT8, DCT16x16, DCT16x8/8x16, DCT32x16/16x32})
     cjxl = 0x5F (pop=6) at d=1,2,3,4 / 0x57 (pop=5) at d=5,6
   cjxl picks 1-2 more buckets, yet its hf_global is 35-50% SMALLER per cell.
   Confirms the cost-gating in our `compute_custom_orders` removes buckets
   whose Lehmer-code cost exceeds expected AC savings.

5. Section attribution per cell (delta = ours - cjxl):
     cell             total Δ    hfglob Δ   passgrp Δ    n_blkclu  used_orders
     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     e6 d=4          +2379       +1683       +225        13 vs 10  0x55 vs 0x5F
     e7 d=3          +2993       +1104       +1000       14 vs 14  0x55 vs 0x5F
     e7 d=4          +4604        +998       +2879       13 vs 13  0x55 vs 0x5F
     e7 d=5          +3523        +953       +2050       10 vs 10  0x55 vs 0x57
     e7 d=6          +3461        +782       +2461        8 vs  8  0x55 vs 0x57
     e7 d=1         -23242       +1153      -30039       14 vs 14  0x55 vs 0x5F
     e7 d=2         -15728        +296      -22416       14 vs 14  0x55 vs 0x5F

6. Within hf_global: dequant Δ = 0 across all cells, ALL the overspend is in
   "perm_etc" (= used_orders + coeff_order Lehmer codes + LZ77 header +
   the hf_dist Decoder header for AC entropy code).

Fix attempts (all REGRESSED — not landed):
==========================================

A. `build_and_write_coeff_orders` LZ77-RLE + enhanced_clustering enabled
   (full libjxl HistogramParams() parity for permutation encoding):
   - codec_wiki_section_attribution_post_fix_2026-05-18.tsv
   - Result: hf_global got +9 to +65 bytes WIDER vs baseline; passgroups
     unchanged; net delta WORSE.
   - Root cause guess: permutation streams are tiny (~80 tokens) — RLE
     header cost dominates any savings, and the extra LZ77 distance
     context adds ANS header overhead.

B. `build_and_write_coeff_orders` enhanced_clustering only (no LZ77):
   - codec_wiki_section_attribution_clusteronly_2026-05-18.tsv
   - Result: hf_global 0 to +21 bytes WIDER vs baseline.
   - Root cause guess: pair-merge has no merge opportunities at 8 contexts
     with ~80 tokens, and the search/select overhead is paid for nothing.

Verdict — wedge is NOT in `build_and_write_coeff_orders`:
========================================================

The dominant cost contributor is the **`hf_dist` AC entropy code header**
(NOT the coefficient orders permutation). `hf_dist` carries:
  - 8-context cluster_map for permutation contexts (small)
  - 1-bit use_prefix_code
  - 2-bit log_alpha_size
  - Per-cluster HybridUintConfig (~10 bits each)
  - Per-cluster ANS histogram (potentially LARGE — `kPrecise` strategy)

At cjxl e7 (kSquirrel), the AC entropy code uses
`ans_histogram_strategy = kApproximate` (`enc_ans_params.h:73` triggers
when `tier >= kSquirrel`). Our code uses `ANSHistogramStrategy::Precise`
unconditionally for VarDCT AC. This means our normalization picks one of
12 split-exponent values; cjxl picks one of 7. The TWO encoders may
converge to the same ans counts (when the underlying histogram favors
the same split), but when they diverge, our Precise encoder picks a more
expensive ANS distribution.

This rules out W44-42's H1-H4 (`ANS clustering parity` / `LZ77 parity` /
`HybridUint parity`). The next chunks should target:

  CH1. ANS histogram strategy: Approximate vs Precise at VarDCT e<9
       (match libjxl kSquirrel default). LOWER risk than disabling
       useful features — kApproximate is libjxl-default behavior.

  CH2. Per-cluster HybridUint config selection: confirm our kNone path
       writes optimal (4,2,0) for ALL clusters (not just the global default).

  CH3. Context-map encoding (simple vs non-simple) at VarDCT AC: confirm
       we always pick the cheaper of the two for the cells in question.

Read-only audit. Workspace will be discarded (no fix shipped).
